  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Satsuma-age",
  "text": "Satsuma-age\n\nPreparation time: 10 minutes\n\nCooking time: 4 minutes\n\nYield: 2\n\nIngredients\n\n150g Pacific cod or pollock (skinned, pin boned, roughly chopped),\n\n1/2 tbsp sake,\n\n1/3 tsp salt,\n\n1/2~1 tbsp potato starch or cornstarch,\n\n1/2 egg,\n\n1/2 tsp ginger root juice,\n\n10g carrot (finely diced),\n\n1/4 onion (finely diced),\n\n1 tsp plain flour,\n\nOil for deep frying,\n\nTo serve\n\nsoy sauce,\n\ngrated ginger root.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Put the fish, sake, and salt in the food processor and process of a few seconds.\n\n2. Add the egg, starch, and ginger root juice and process briefly.\n\n3. Put the onion and carrot in a bowl and mix in the flour.\n\n4. Mix the fish mixture with the vegetable mixture.\n\n5. Divide into 6 and deep fry for 4 minutes.\n\n6. Serve with the ginger and soy sauce.",
  "prepTime": "PT10M",
  "cookTime": "PT4M",
  "recipeYield": "2",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "150g Pacific cod or pollock (skinned, pin boned, roughly chopped),",
